<title>USA: Consumers shuts 780 MW Palisades nuke plant.</title>
<headline>Consumers shuts 780 MW Palisades nuke plant.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Consumers Power Co shut its 780 megawatt (MW) Palisades nuclear power plant Sunday for repairs, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said Monday.</p>
<p>The NRC, in its daily status report, said the generating station, in South Haven, Mich., was taken off line to correct a &quot;broken connector in isophase bus.&quot;</p>
<p>Palisades, which was running near full power before the shutdown, was kept in hot shutdown and could resume service as early as today, NRC said.</p>
<p>Consumers Power, a subsidiary of CMS Energy, is the owner and operator of the plant.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1622))</p>
